# KnowNote deliberately uses npm, not pnpm.
#
# electron-builder collects production dependencies with its own node-module
# collector, and that collector is built around npm's flat-ish node_modules
# layout. Against pnpm's virtual store it silently dropped transitive
# dependencies (jsdom -> whatwg-url -> tr46, http-proxy-agent -> debug -> ms),
# which is how v1.2.1 shipped an app.asar that crashed with MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
# See https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder/issues/10064.
#
# The previous workaround lived in this file (shamefully-hoist=true,
# node-linker=isolated) plus five hand-promoted transitive dependencies in
# package.json. Both are gone: a flat node_modules makes collection
# well-defined, and `allowMissingDependencies: false` in electron-builder.yml
# turns any remaining miss into a hard build failure instead of a runtime crash.
#
# Do not reintroduce pnpm-only options here (shamefully-hoist, node-linker,
# onlyBuiltDependencies, ...). npm warns about unknown project config and they
# only ever papered over the collector.

# Electron / electron-builder binaries are fetched from the official sources so
# release artifacts stay reproducible and verifiable. Developers behind a slow
# link can opt in locally instead of changing this file:
#   export ELECTRON_MIRROR=https://npmmirror.com/mirrors/electron/
#   export ELECTRON_BUILDER_BINARIES_MIRROR=https://npmmirror.com/mirrors/electron-builder-binaries/
